--- !u!114 &67584702
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 67584700}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 30e8e37d88289204784a0442b3c88612, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  steps:
  - Connect (220 VAC) terminal and the neutral path (N) of all used modules to the
    (220 VAC) terminal and the neutral path (N) of the main board.
  - Connect an Ethernet cable from the PV Solar Panel (Comm. Out) to the Main Control
    Board module (Comm. In).
  - Connect (+VE) and (-VE) Battery Input terminals of the Off-Grid Inverter module
    to (+VE) and (-VE) terminals of the Battery 24V/ 9AH module.
  - Connect (L) and (N) AC Output terminals of the Off-Grid Inverter module to (L)
    and (N) terminals of the AC Halogen Lamp module.
  - Connect (+VE) and (-VE) DC Input terminals of the Off-Grid Inverter module to
    (+VE) and (-VE) terminals of the PV Solar Panel Output module.
  - Release the emergency stop button on the main board.
  - Raise the circuit breaker (C.B) of the main board.
  - Switch on the main board ON/OFF switch.
  - Release the emergency button of the PV Solar Panel.
  - Switch on the PV Solar Panel ON/OFF.
  - Switch the Run/Stop selector to Run state.
  - Switch to the control software on the connected PC.
  - "Connect (L) and (N) terminals of the main frame \u201Cgrid\u201D with off-grid
    inverter.\r\n\r\n\u2022\tConnect (N) terminal of the off-grid inverter module
    \u201CAC input\u201D to the (N) terminal of the main frame \u201Cgrid\u201D.\r\n\u2022\t
    Connect (L) terminal of the off-grid inverter module \u201CAC\r\ninput\u201D
    to the (L) terminal of the main frame \u201Cgrid\u201D.\r\n"
  - You have finished! You can now select another experiment.
  popups:
  - afterStep: 2
    text: Always connect the battery before connecting PV panels or AC sources to
      the charge controller.
  - afterStep: 4
    text: Always ensure emergency buttons are released before powering on any module.
  - afterStep: 5
    text: Always ensure emergency buttons are released before powering on any module.
  - afterStep: 11
    text: Observe that the battery now supplies the AC load.
  - afterStep: 11
    text: You'll notice that when PV panels share the load with battery, the battery
      discharge current will be reduced.
  - afterStep: 12
    text: "As soon as you connect the AC input, wait for a while (5sec) until you
      hear a (Tick) sound from the off -grid inverter, this means that the inverter
      starts the conversion. You will notice that the battery begins to charge and
      the current sign becomes positive \u201C+\u201D. The AC input (grid) and the
      PVs input are sharing with each other\r\nto supply the whole system with power
      as supplying the AC load, DC load and charging the battery.\r\n"
  - afterStep: 12
    text: "Note that you can: \r\n\tExport all recorded measurements to an Excel
      sheet by clicking the \"Export Data\" icon.\r\n\tSave the screen by pressing
      the \"Save Screen\" icon.\r\n\tClear the graph using the \"Clear\" icon.\r\n"
  stepItemPrefab: {fileID: 6570533322573217691, guid: cd25d304eaf4809488e7c6b299d13404, type: 3}
