--- !u!114 &395034151
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 395034149}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 30e8e37d88289204784a0442b3c88612, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  steps:
  - Connect (220 VAC) terminal and the neutral path (N) of all used modules to the
    (220 VAC) terminal and the neutral path (N) of the main board.
  - Connect an Ethernet cable from the PV Solar Panel (Comm. Out) to the Main Control
    Board module (Comm. In).
  - Connect (+VE) and (-VE) Battery terminals of the PWM Solar Charge Controller
    module to (+VE) and (-VE) terminals of the Battery 24V/ 9AH module.
  - Connect (+VE) and (-VE) DC Load terminals of the PWM Solar Charge Controller
    module to (+VE) and (-VE) terminals of the DC LED Lamp module
  - Connect (+VE) and (-VE) Solar Panel terminals of the PWM Solar Charge Controller
    module to (+VE) and (-VE) terminals of the PV Solar Panel Output module
  - Release the emergency stop button on the main board.
  - Raise the circuit breaker (C.B) of the main board.
  - Switch on the main board ON/OFF switch.
  - Release the emergency button of the PV Solar Panel.
  - Switch on the PV Solar Panel ON/OFF.
  - Switch the Run/Stop selector to Run state.
  - Operate the DC load using the load control button on the PWM charge controller.
  - Switch to the control software on the connected PC.
  - You have finished! You can now select another experiment.
  popups:
  - afterStep: 2
    text: Always connect the battery before connecting PV panels or AC sources to
      the charge controller.
  - afterStep: 4
    text: Always ensure emergency buttons are released before powering on any module.
  - afterStep: 12
    text: Observe that the battery now supplies power to both the DC load and the
      PWM controller.
  - afterStep: 12
    text: You'll notice that when PV panels share the load with battery, the battery
      discharge current will be reduced.
  - afterStep: 12
    text: "Note that you can: \r\n\tExport all recorded measurements to an Excel
      sheet by clicking the \"Export Data\" icon.\r\n\tSave the screen by pressing
      the \"Save Screen\" icon.\r\n\tClear the graph using the \"Clear\" icon\r"
  stepItemPrefab: {fileID: 6570533322573217691, guid: cd25d304eaf4809488e7c6b299d13404, type: 3}
  contentParent: {fileID: 395034150}
